> Also, when you identify a rustproof item, why doesn't it say something along
> the lines of 'a rustproof +0 longsword'?  I mean, it's quite obvious what
> the Shimmering golden shield is (after the 1st identify), so why in the world
> not?

I added this patch to my otherwise standard 3.0j installation.  I also sent it
in to the dev team, who tell me that they are trying to get it into 3.1.

The patch is: if an item is made of metel, is rustproof, and is known to be
rustproof, then the string "rustproof " appears when the item is listed in
inventory ("a blessed rustproof +4 longsword named Excalibur").  Further, to
keep the user interface orthogonal, rustproof items may be wished for by
asking for them the way they appear in inventory.  An item is known to be
rustproof either if it has been identified or the player has seen one of the
characteristic messages like "your %s is not affected!".  But the shimmering
gold field message does not identify the rustproof status.  Naturally, I'm
proud of the patch.  It's made the game a lot more fun for me.  Hold your
breath!

